  "digest": "# Transportation & Logistics \u2014 sector digest, ISO 2026-W46\n\n**Coverage changes.** One sign-off batch on 13 Nov returned BIRD, CASS, SMDR, TMAS and ELPI once each; four cleared after revision and published, ELPI went back twice and was parked on exhausted rounds. Published: BIRD BUY, target Rp1,714 (+32.9% to price); CASS BUY, Rp2,717 (+53.1%); SMDR BUY, Rp870 (+175.9%); TMAS ADD, Rp127 (+16.6%). GMFI's 13 Nov update (BUY, Rp125) is back at sign-off on the 22.03bn-share rights issue filed 13 Nov, with the dilution bridge now sourced and the target cut. ASSA, BLOG, HATM and MITI remain at draft \u2014 five names in flight including GMFI.\n\n**Deck moves.** No forecast changes this week. Macro was last reviewed 7 Nov: USD/IDR FY2026E 17,570, spot 18,190 on 13 Nov. Oil was last reviewed 26 Oct: Brent FY2026E 96.0, spot 95.89 on 13 Nov. Airlines and shipping read both decks; logistics reads macro only.\n\n**Material news.**\n- GMFI plans a rights issue of 22bn Series B shares for up to US$59.41m [7ec6b36c38a1f41d]; parent GIAA's Rp6.21trn rights issue is partly an inbreng of GMFI shares, so the two interlock [1daa1bfed26b196b].\n- BPS: domestic air passengers fell 12.39% yoy in September 2026, while rail, sea and ferry passengers rose [7c7f7d6cca83aa32].\n- The government budgeted Rp883bn for Christmas-New Year air, rail and sea ticket discounts [a4d59c3d80b25d92].\n- ASSA obtained a Rp300bn CIMB Niaga facility for working capital and vehicle procurement [a283da0bf197150e].\n\n**What to watch.** GMFI's sign-off verdict and whether the rights-issue dilution is reflected consistently with GIAA's inbreng. ELPI's park goes to the Director. Four drafts (ASSA, BLOG, HATM, MITI) need to clear. Nataru demand data and discount uptake will test the airline volume case. Brent spot is tracking the FY2026E 96 path and USD/IDR sits above the 18,080 WACC basis; a deck refresh would change airline and shipping inputs.\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*\n",
  "digest_file": "fund record"
